      "bbox": {
        "l": 106.377996,
        "t": 452.8957760000001,
        "r": 541.5556139999997,
        "b": 410.0041529281769
      },
      "content": "When  the  alarm  generally  has  occurred,  the  screen  will  be  converted  to  the  alarm automatically  and  the  message  \"AL\"  or  \"A/B\"(battery  alarm)  flashed  in  the  lower  right  of screen."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_1238",
      "reading_order": 1586,
      "section": "3-9-3. Alarm Indicator",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 106.37699400000002,
        "t": 384.9160880000001,
        "r": 300.54255,
        "b": 325.0445729281769
      },
      "content": "The  upper  side  (ALARM)  of  alarm diagnostic  screen  indicates  the  NC alarm and the lower  (MESSAGE) displays up to 4 PC alarms. ft1"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_1239",
      "reading_order": 1587,
      "section": "3-9-3. Alarm Indicator",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 106.37699400000002,
        "t": 299.8963880000001,
        "r": 303.1978499999999,
        "b": 240.02487292817682
      },
      "content": "To delete the alarm, remove the cause and then press the RESET button. If the alarm has not been deleted by pressing the RESET key, it will remain"
    },
